True. I msut agree on that Crossfire is one of the best games in this genre.
However, there's one thing with Crossfire that I don't like, and that is the
lack of a goal in the game. At low-levels it is fun, trying to get those
plussed armours and artefatcs, and trying to defeat that Dragon or whatever.
But once you are level 25, you almost for sure have the best equipment,
can slaughter almost any monster and so on, it gets kinda boring.

Another thing that I would like to see in Crossfire is some kind of party
system, currently you can help to kill a monster, but only one of you gets
the exp for it.

But, as Jerry said, the game is still under development (What net-game
isn't? ;-) ) , and these things will probably be added later.

I am not discouraging you from trying the game, it's awesome, and it has
a great potential of developing into the ultimate game.

Thank you for bringing us this game, you folks in the Crossfire dev-team!

